Dialogue: 0,0:00:12.43,0:00:18.80,EN,,0,0,0,,{\fad(200,200)}Even though I’ve been stretching myself as far as I can
Dialogue: 0,0:00:18.86,0:00:25.30,EN,,0,0,0,,{\fad(200,200)}I just can’t do it well when I’m in front of you
Dialogue: 0,0:00:25.30,0:00:30.25,EN,,0,0,0,,{\fad(200,200)}My feelings are changing faster
Dialogue: 0,0:00:30.91,0:00:33.47,EN,,0,0,0,,{\fad(200,200)}Than soda losing its fizz
Dialogue: 0,0:00:33.47,0:00:40.43,EN,,0,0,0,,{\fad(200,200)}I haven’t even noticed it myself yet
Dialogue: 0,0:00:40.43,0:00:41.27,EN,,0,0,0,,{\fad(200,200)}Hey
Dialogue: 0,0:00:41.27,0:00:54.03,EN,,0,0,0,,{\fad(200,200)}It’s a little different from the future I wished for in the beginning, but
Dialogue: 0,0:00:54.03,0:01:06.87,EN,,0,0,0,,{\fad(200,200)}In the end, I don’t need anything—just stay by my side
Dialogue: 0,0:01:06.87,0:01:13.17,EN,,0,0,0,,{\fad(200,200)}Clumsy and always missing each other, overthinking everything—that’s just how we are
Dialogue: 0,0:01:13.17,0:01:19.18,EN,,0,0,0,,{\fad(200,200)}Saying “I can’t say it” over and over—how selfish is that?
Dialogue: 0,0:01:19.57,0:01:25.89,EN,,0,0,0,,{\fad(200,200)}Even if I think I want a tomorrow where you’re there, I can’t change it
Dialogue: 0,0:01:26.03,0:01:30.82,EN,,0,0,0,,{\fad(200,200)}I have to tell you
